  {
    "episode_id": 84887,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84887.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "I would say that you should pray to God to give you a passion. Because if you have a passion, then it's never work, it's fun, it's exciting. I wake up every day, oh boy, I get to go to work on my infrastructure projects and for the great city of New York and the great country that we live in. I wake up and say a prayer and thank God that I was born in America, that I'm American and I can be part of this great country. All of our ancestors came as immigrants, including mine, but it is a great, great country. And I would say that if you have something you really want to do that you feel you can contribute and be part of, then it's always fun. And it's exciting. And I truly do believe that there is no profession that is more rewarding than public service if it's done, honestly. with great commitment and fairness. So I am grateful to have the opportunity to serve three boroughs in the United States Congress of",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
